-- and a rate given by its measured values either side of where it crosses: below the temperature tc the
-- order of magnitude is lo and at or above it hi. This is not Eyring's relation, which wants a logarithm
-- the core does not have; it is the measurement, with the crossing where the measurement puts it. A
-- barrier determines the crossing and the crossing is what a variable-temperature experiment reports.
rate-step : Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat
rate-step tc hi lo t = case leb tc t of true → hi; false → lo
